/* lookup4:

  Test if GAMMA state cache for Lookup with parameters have unique/per-argument
  cache entries.

  The plan:
  - Creates a loop to iterate over the arguments 0 and 1 of the parametric Lookup `externalVar`.
  - A variable counter and an assignment are used to track the Lookup argument.
  - A couple of disjoint print commands are defined to execute whether the Lookup in their StartCondition is known or not.
    NOTE: If one of the print commands is executed, the other is skipped so that they can synchronize with after the macro
          step induced by the print command execution.
  The script:
  - Initializes only the Lookup instance externalVar(0) to -10.
  - Keeps the Lookup instance externalVar(1) undefined.
  - Ticks the time for 10,11,12, and 13.

  Expected behavior:
  - Output:
    ```
    [isKnownPrint] time:  10  argument counter:  0 externalVar:  -10
    [isUnknownPrint] time:  11  argument counter:  1  externalVar:  [unknown_value]
    [isKnownPrint] time:  12  argument counter:  0 externalVar:  -10
    ```
  - When the time ticks 13 the ExitCondition of the root should force all the nodes to transition towards FINISHED.

  Conclusions:
  - The executive keeps a cache entry per instance of parametric Lookups.

 */
        Command pprint(...);
Real    Lookup  externalVar(Integer);
Real    Lookup  time;

lookup4: Concurrence
{
   Integer counter = 0;
   Exit Lookup(time) > 12;

   lookupOnChangePrint : Concurrence {
      Repeat true;
      counter = (counter + 1) mod 2;
      isUnknownPrint: {
        Start !isKnown(Lookup(externalVar(counter)));
        Skip isKnownPrint.state == EXECUTING;
        pprint("[isUnknownPrint] time: ", Lookup(time), " argument counter: ", counter, " externalVar: ", Lookup(externalVar(counter)));
      }
      isKnownPrint: {
        Start isKnown(Lookup(externalVar(counter)));
        Skip isUnknownPrint.state == EXECUTING;
        pprint("[isKnownPrint] time: ", Lookup(time), " argument counter: ", counter, "externalVar: ", Lookup(externalVar(counter)));
      }
   }
}